WEBVTT

1
00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:37.599
- Potts?
- Yeah.

2
00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:39.439
Bill Potts.

3
00:01:39.440 --> 00:01:41.199
You wanted to see me.

4
00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:43.399
Er. you're not a student
at this university.

5
00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:45.999
- No. I work in the canteen.
- Yeah. but you come to my lectures.

6
00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:48.919
No. I don't. I never do that.

7
00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:50.199
I've seen you.

8
00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:53.079
Love your lectures.
They're totally awesome.

9
00:01:53.080 --> 00:01:55.479
Why d'you come to my lectures
when you're not a student?

10
00:01:55.480 --> 00:01:57.999
OK. so my first day
here. in the canteen.

11
00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:01.439
I was on chips. There was this girl.
Student. Beautiful.

12
00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:04.359
Like a model. only with
talking and thinking.

13
00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:08.439
She looked at you and you perved.
Every time. automatic. Like physics.

14
00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:12.279
Eye contact. perversion.
So I gave her extra chips.

15
00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:16.039
Every time. extra chips. Like a
reward for all the perversion.

16
00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:19.039
Every day. got myself
on chips. rewarded her.

17
00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:22.039
Then. finally. finally.
she looked at me.

18
00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:25.439
Like she'd noticed. actually
noticed. all the extra chips.

19
00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:27.519
Do you know what I realised?

20
00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:28.680
She was fat.

21
00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:31.240
I'd fatted her.

22
00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:36.279
But that's life. isn't it?
Beauty or chips. I like chips.

23
00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:38.440
So did she. So that's OK.

24
00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:41.759
And how does that in any way explain

25
00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:43.919
why you keep coming to my lectures?

26
00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:47.879
Yeah. it doesn't really. does it? I
was hoping something would develop.

27
00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:49.919
What's that?

28
00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:51.400
A police telephone box?

29
00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:55.239
- Yeah.
- Did you build it from a kit?

30
00:02:55.240 --> 00:02:57.799
- No. it came like that.
- Then how did you get it in here?

31
00:02:57.800 --> 00:03:00.079
The door's too small and
so are the windows.

32
00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:03.319
I had the window and a part of the
wall taken out and it was lifted in.

33
00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:06.799
- What. with a crane?
- Yeah. with a crane.

34
00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:08.079
It's heavier than it looks.

35
00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:11.399
- Why do you keep coming to my lectures?
- Because I like them.

36
00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:13.920
Everybody likes them. they're amazing.

37
00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:17.018
- Why me?
- Why you what?

38
00:03:17.020 --> 00:03:19.321
Plenty of people come to your
lectures that aren't supposed to.

39
00:03:19.323 --> 00:03:21.432
- Why pick on me?
- Well. I noticed you.

40
00:03:21.713 --> 00:03:23.705
Yeah. but why?

41
00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:28.079
Well. most people when don't
understand something. they frown.

42
00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:29.200
You...

43
00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:31.520
smile.

44
00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:35.759
I'll tell you what I don't understand.

45
00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:38.639
You've been lecturing here
for a long time. 50 years.

46
00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:40.079
some people say.

47
00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:42.079
Nabeela in the office says over 70.

48
00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:44.479
And you're thinking. "Well.
he doesn't look old enough"?

49
00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:47.319
No. I'm wondering what you're
supposed to be lecturing on.

50
00:03:47.320 --> 00:03:50.399
It's like the university let
you do whatever you like.

51
00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:53.199
One time. you were going to give
a lecture on quantum physics.

52
00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:55.919
- You talked about poetry.
- Poetry. physics. same thing.

53
00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:57.399
How is it the same?

54
00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:59.839
Because of the rhymes. What are
you doing at this university?

55
00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:02.560
- I always wanted to come here.
- Yeah. to serve chips?

56
00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:06.399
So anyway. am I nearly done?

57
00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:07.799
Do you want to be?

58
00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:09.080
See ya.

59
00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:13.919
You ever get less than a
first. then it's over.

60
00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:15.680
- You what?
- A first.

61
00:04:16.760 --> 00:04:20.119
- Every time. or I stop immediately.
- Stop what?

62
00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:21.720
Being your personal tutor.

63
00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:25.639
But I'm not a student.

64
00:04:25.640 --> 00:04:27.359
I'm not part of the university.

65
00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:29.279
I never even applied.

66
00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:30.479
We'll sort all that out later.

67
00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:32.479
You kind of have to
sort that out earlier.

68
00:04:32.480 --> 00:04:34.720
Leave it with me. I'm
assuming that it's a yes.

69
00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:39.399
- Yes.
- I'll see you at 6pm every weekday.

70
00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:41.639
I don't care who's dying
never. ever be late.

71
00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:43.600
I'm very particular about time.

72
00:04:46.360 --> 00:04:47.840
Um...

73
00:04:49.360 --> 00:04:51.360
People just call you the Doctor?

74
00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:54.079
What do I call you?

75
00:04:54.080 --> 00:04:55.959
The Doctor.

76
00:04:55.960 --> 00:04:59.320
But Doctor's not a name. I
can't just call you Doctor.

77
00:05:00.840 --> 00:05:02.200
Doctor what?

78
00:05:46.560 --> 00:05:48.879
Time! Time doesn't pass.

79
00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:53.280
The passage of time is an illusion.
and life is the magician.

80
00:05:55.440 --> 00:05:58.880
Because life only lets you
see one day at a time.

81
00:06:04.040 --> 00:06:05.599
You remember being alive yesterday.

82
00:06:05.600 --> 00:06:07.479
you hope you're going
to be alive tomorrow.

83
00:06:07.480 --> 00:06:11.359
So it feels like you're
travelling from one to the other.

84
00:06:11.360 --> 00:06:13.959
But nobody's moving anywhere.

85
00:06:13.960 --> 00:06:16.639
Movies don't really move.

86
00:06:16.640 --> 00:06:19.519
They're just pictures.
lots and lots of pictures.

87
00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:22.959
All of them still. none of them moving.
Just frozen moments.

88
00:06:26.200 --> 00:06:30.479
But if you experience those
pictures one after the other.

89
00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:32.240
then everything comes alive.

90
00:06:36.720 --> 00:06:39.480
- Am I on time?
- That's a very big question.

91
00:06:46.120 --> 00:06:48.479
You know you're my foster mum?

92
00:06:48.480 --> 00:06:50.519
He's like my foster tutor.

93
00:06:50.520 --> 00:06:53.079
Am I going to have to break
every bone in his body?

94
00:06:53.080 --> 00:06:54.719
It's not like that.

95
00:06:54.720 --> 00:06:56.720
You need to keep your eye on men.

96
00:06:58.720 --> 00:07:01.119
Men aren't where I
keep my eye. actually.

97
00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:03.240
Imagine if time all happened at once...

98
00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:09.680
every moment of your life
laid out around you...

99
00:07:11.800 --> 00:07:15.919
like a city. Streets full
of buildings made of days.

100
00:07:15.920 --> 00:07:19.119
The day you were born. the day you die.

101
00:07:19.120 --> 00:07:22.439
The day you fall in love.
the day that love ends.

102
00:07:22.440 --> 00:07:27.399
A whole city built from triumph
and heartbreak and boredom

103
00:07:27.400 --> 00:07:30.079
and laughter and cutting your toenails.

104
00:07:30.080 --> 00:07:32.559
It's the best place you will ever be.

105
00:07:35.320 --> 00:07:40.320
Time is a structure
relative to ourselves.

106
00:07:44.560 --> 00:07:45.799
I'll get them in.

107
00:07:45.800 --> 00:07:53.200
Time is the space made by our lives
where we stand together. forever.

108
00:07:54.720 --> 00:07:57.880
Time And Relative Dimension...

109
00:07:59.520 --> 00:08:03.120
In Space.

110
00:08:04.520 --> 00:08:06.239
It means life.

111
00:08:09.120 --> 00:08:10.880
- Just chips. yeah?
- Please.

112
00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:31.320
Ooh!

113
00:09:03.360 --> 00:09:06.400
So you're tutoring her. then?

114
00:09:07.400 --> 00:09:09.799
- Yes. I am.
- Why?

115
00:09:09.800 --> 00:09:11.239
Why not?

116
00:09:11.240 --> 00:09:12.960
You're not supposed to get involved.

117
00:09:14.000 --> 00:09:16.119
What are you teaching her anyway?

118
00:09:16.120 --> 00:09:17.479
Everything.

119
00:09:17.480 --> 00:09:19.679
Well. how can you teach
anyone everything?

120
00:09:19.680 --> 00:09:21.320
Because everything rhymes.

121
00:09:23.240 --> 00:09:28.399
Links apple and alpha.
synchronous and diverging...

122
00:09:29.600 --> 00:09:31.159
Yeah. you want to turn that.

123
00:09:33.960 --> 00:09:35.640
You want to rotate it.

124
00:09:48.640 --> 00:09:51.519
The door upstairs. how did
you set the security?

125
00:09:51.520 --> 00:09:52.840
Friends only.

126
00:09:59.920 --> 00:10:02.519
So turn it. and then it'll...

127
00:10:02.520 --> 00:10:04.040
- I'm turning it.
- All right.

128
00:10:31.240 --> 00:10:33.840
- You OK?
- Yeah. I'm fine.

129
00:10:38.880 --> 00:10:41.439
Sorry. can I ask what's
that in your eye?

130
00:10:41.440 --> 00:10:43.719
It's just a defect in the iris.

131
00:10:43.720 --> 00:10:46.039
- Looks like a star.
- Well. it's a defect.

132
00:10:46.040 --> 00:10:47.758
At least it's a defect
that looks like a star.

133
00:10:47.760 --> 00:10:48.799
I'm getting it fixed.

134
00:10:50.840 --> 00:10:52.280
OK.

135
00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:59.200
Sorry. None of my business. but are
you freaking out about something?

136
00:11:03.760 --> 00:11:07.639
Please. You can say no.
Would you come with me?

137
00:11:07.640 --> 00:11:08.959
Can I show you something?

138
00:11:08.960 --> 00:11:10.280
God. yes.

139
00:11:12.560 --> 00:11:15.599
- I love this place. don't you?
- Hate it.

140
00:11:15.600 --> 00:11:18.759
- Why?
- I don't know. I just do.

141
00:11:18.760 --> 00:11:21.479
Everywhere I go I just want to leave.

142
00:11:21.480 --> 00:11:22.720
Can I come too?

143
00:11:24.280 --> 00:11:25.600
Maybe.

144
00:11:37.920 --> 00:11:39.919
There's a puddle over there.

145
00:11:39.920 --> 00:11:41.799
But it hasn't rained for a week.

146
00:11:41.800 --> 00:11:45.439
Yeah. but. well. you know. half
the students here are blokes...

147
00:11:45.440 --> 00:11:46.919
Go and look in it.

148
00:11:46.920 --> 00:11:49.280
- You want me to look in a puddle?
- Please.

149
00:11:57.880 --> 00:11:59.160
OK. I'm looking.

150
00:12:00.600 --> 00:12:03.000
- What am I looking at?
- Your reflection.

151
00:12:05.280 --> 00:12:08.439
- Yep. There it is.
- Do you see what's wrong with it?

152
00:12:08.440 --> 00:12:10.919
My name's Bill. by the way.

153
00:12:10.920 --> 00:12:12.319
Heather.

154
00:12:12.320 --> 00:12:14.319
Can you see what's wrong?

155
00:12:14.320 --> 00:12:16.120
Nothing. It just looks like me.

156
00:12:19.880 --> 00:12:21.120
What is that?

157
00:12:23.200 --> 00:12:25.119
That's me. that's my face. but...

158
00:12:25.120 --> 00:12:27.000
It's wrong.

159
00:12:29.480 --> 00:12:32.600
- Hey!
- Sorry. Some other time.

160
00:12:34.080 --> 00:12:35.440
Promise?

161
00:12:40.320 --> 00:12:42.920
Pilot is located.

162
00:12:44.560 --> 00:12:47.640
Link is established.

163
00:13:08.240 --> 00:13:10.679
It's a rug.

164
00:13:10.680 --> 00:13:12.559
Haven't got you anything.

165
00:13:12.560 --> 00:13:14.600
It's OK. it was cheap.

166
00:13:22.800 --> 00:13:24.919
Going anywhere for Christmas?

167
00:13:24.920 --> 00:13:26.359
I never go anywhere.

168
00:13:26.360 --> 00:13:28.079
That's not true.

169
00:13:28.080 --> 00:13:29.879
You go places. I can tell.

170
00:13:29.880 --> 00:13:31.279
My mum always said.

171
00:13:31.280 --> 00:13:33.919
"With some people you can smell
the wind in their clothes."

172
00:13:35.200 --> 00:13:38.320
She sounds... nice.

173
00:13:39.440 --> 00:13:41.079
She died when I was a baby.

174
00:13:41.080 --> 00:13:43.120
Yeah.

175
00:13:46.200 --> 00:13:49.799
If she died when you were a
baby. when did she say that?

176
00:13:49.800 --> 00:13:51.200
In my head.

177
00:13:53.280 --> 00:13:57.079
I'm supposed to look like
her. but I don't really know.

178
00:13:57.080 --> 00:13:59.399
There's hardly any photographs.

179
00:13:59.400 --> 00:14:01.480
She hated having her picture taken.

180
00:14:02.560 --> 00:14:05.760
But if someone's gone.
do pictures really help?

181
00:14:09.520 --> 00:14:12.359
I thought you'd enjoy choosing
something for yourself.

182
00:14:12.360 --> 00:14:14.800
as you're always passing judgments.

183
00:14:16.360 --> 00:14:18.399
I hope you didn't spend
too much on this.

184
00:14:18.400 --> 00:14:20.599
Nah. This should cover it.

185
00:14:20.600 --> 00:14:22.119
What's that?

186
00:14:22.120 --> 00:14:24.119
Ooh. I found that at the
back of the cupboard

187
00:14:24.120 --> 00:14:27.440
with all your old stuff. Just
photographs of your mum.

188
00:14:28.560 --> 00:14:30.120
I didn't know we had 'em.

189
00:15:18.080 --> 00:15:19.519
Happy new term!

190
00:15:19.520 --> 00:15:21.120
With you in a moment.

191
00:15:26.600 --> 00:15:28.999
You said you needed a
crane to lift your box.

192
00:15:29.000 --> 00:15:30.640
Sorry. what did you say?

193
00:15:57.800 --> 00:15:59.080
Hey!

194
00:16:02.280 --> 00:16:04.000
Still making eyes at a puddle?

195
00:16:05.400 --> 00:16:08.199
Did you ever work out what was
wrong with your reflection?

196
00:16:08.200 --> 00:16:09.839
Nah.

197
00:16:09.840 --> 00:16:11.600
Come round. I'll show you.

198
00:16:12.720 --> 00:16:13.960
Promise you won't go?

199
00:16:15.280 --> 00:16:16.600
Promise.

200
00:16:37.040 --> 00:16:38.519
OK.

201
00:16:38.520 --> 00:16:40.120
Yeah. no worries.

202
00:16:42.720 --> 00:16:47.000
Pilot confirmed. Pilot engaged.

203
00:16:56.920 --> 00:16:58.280
What's wrong?

204
00:17:00.480 --> 00:17:03.759
She said it was a defect.
but what kind of defect

205
00:17:03.760 --> 00:17:05.280
puts a star in your eye?

206
00:17:06.480 --> 00:17:10.119
But that doesn't even matter
because she was right.

207
00:17:10.120 --> 00:17:13.839
There was something wrong when
you looked in the puddle.

208
00:17:13.840 --> 00:17:17.279
That was definitely my face.
I see my face all the time.

209
00:17:17.280 --> 00:17:19.119
I've never liked it.
it's all over the place.

210
00:17:19.120 --> 00:17:21.799
It's always doing expressions
when I'm trying to be enigmatic.

211
00:17:21.800 --> 00:17:23.839
I know my face.

212
00:17:23.840 --> 00:17:27.080
and there was something wrong
with my face in the puddle.

213
00:17:28.640 --> 00:17:30.840
What could be wrong with your own face?

214
00:17:43.360 --> 00:17:45.040
Doctor!

215
00:17:49.200 --> 00:17:50.880
Doctor!

216
00:18:00.160 --> 00:18:02.079
- Why do you run like that?
- Like what?

217
00:18:02.080 --> 00:18:04.359
Like a penguin with its arse on fire.

218
00:18:04.360 --> 00:18:05.720
Ergonomics.

219
00:18:06.680 --> 00:18:08.359
That's my face. yeah?

220
00:18:08.360 --> 00:18:10.039
You seem a bit flexible on the subject.

221
00:18:10.040 --> 00:18:11.559
You've no idea.

222
00:18:11.560 --> 00:18:13.600
Maybe it's got to do with
that thing in her eye.

223
00:18:13.602 --> 00:18:14.280
How?

224
00:18:14.281 --> 00:18:16.481
Maybe she's like...
affected by something.

225
00:18:16.483 --> 00:18:17.320
Like what?

226
00:18:17.321 --> 00:18:20.519
I don't know. Look. I know you
know lots of stuff about.

227
00:18:20.520 --> 00:18:23.120
well. basically everything.
but do you know any sci-fi?

228
00:18:28.800 --> 00:18:30.199
Go on.

229
00:18:30.200 --> 00:18:33.079
Well. what if she's... possessed.

230
00:18:33.080 --> 00:18:35.119
Something like that.

231
00:18:35.120 --> 00:18:36.719
Possessed by what?

232
00:18:36.720 --> 00:18:38.519
I don't know.

233
00:18:38.520 --> 00:18:42.839
I saw this thing on Netflix.
Lizards in people's brains.

234
00:18:42.840 --> 00:18:45.039
Right. So. you meet a girl
with a discoloured iris

235
00:18:45.040 --> 00:18:48.319
and your first thought is she
might have a lizard in her brain?

236
00:18:48.320 --> 00:18:50.520
I can see I'm going to
have to up my game.

237
00:18:52.840 --> 00:18:55.486
What?

238
00:18:56.400 --> 00:18:59.840
- What is it. what?
- I get it. I see it.

239
00:19:00.840 --> 00:19:03.479
It was easy for your
friend because of her eye.

240
00:19:03.480 --> 00:19:05.079
Because it gives her special powers?

241
00:19:05.080 --> 00:19:07.960
No! Because her face
isn't symmetrical. Look!

242
00:19:10.400 --> 00:19:11.840
Look into the puddle.

243
00:19:12.880 --> 00:19:16.599
Your face looks wrong.
because it looks right.

244
00:19:16.600 --> 00:19:19.519
What's the one thing you never see
when you look in a reflection?

245
00:19:19.520 --> 00:19:22.720
Your face. You never see your
face the right way round.

246
00:19:23.960 --> 00:19:27.039
Right. Look for a freckle
or a funny tooth.

247
00:19:27.040 --> 00:19:29.199
- Something that's not symmetrical.
- My badge!

248
00:19:29.200 --> 00:19:32.679
See. your friend saw it
straightaway because of her eye.

249
00:19:32.680 --> 00:19:35.640
But... it's moving like a reflection.

250
00:19:42.520 --> 00:19:45.479
It's not reflecting you.

251
00:19:45.480 --> 00:19:46.920
It's mimicking you.

252
00:19:48.520 --> 00:19:51.560
There's something in the
water pretending to be you.

253
00:19:53.160 --> 00:19:56.400
Of course. it isn't water.

254
00:19:58.440 --> 00:20:01.159
Now what are these? Let's have a look.

255
00:20:01.160 --> 00:20:02.440
What are they?

256
00:20:03.680 --> 00:20:04.720
Scorch marks.

257
00:20:05.760 --> 00:20:07.000
Interesting.

258
00:20:14.000 --> 00:20:15.200
Right. you.

259
00:20:17.040 --> 00:20:19.399
- Let's get you on the bus!
- The what. the bus?

260
00:20:19.400 --> 00:20:21.599
Tutorial's over. take the night off.

261
00:20:21.600 --> 00:20:24.399
It's all cancelled. Go
and be a proper student

262
00:20:24.400 --> 00:20:26.599
texts. snogging. a vegan wrap.

263
00:20:26.600 --> 00:20:28.319
But what about the puddle?

264
00:20:28.320 --> 00:20:32.440
It's just some freak optical effect.
I'm bored already.

265
00:20:34.360 --> 00:20:38.600
Passenger selected.
Pursuit engaged.

266
00:20:53.320 --> 00:20:54.519
Hey!

267
00:20:54.520 --> 00:20:56.880
I'll make you a cuppa for the bath.

268
00:21:12.560 --> 00:21:13.799
Hey.

269
00:21:13.800 --> 00:21:15.639
Sorry I'm not there. love.

270
00:21:15.640 --> 00:21:18.439
but I think we both know
it's time I treated myself.

271
00:21:18.440 --> 00:21:20.039
Are you with Neville?

272
00:21:20.040 --> 00:21:23.519
Why would I be back with
Neville after last time?

273
00:21:23.520 --> 00:21:25.959
Why do you think I'm such an idiot?

274
00:21:25.960 --> 00:21:27.640
Well. you're calling from his phone.

275
00:21:30.560 --> 00:21:33.279
Is there someone staying
here in the flat?

276
00:21:33.280 --> 00:21:35.240
Of course not. no. What
are you talking about?

277
00:21:36.440 --> 00:21:40.240
Er... nothing. never mind.
I'll see you tomorrow.

278
00:21:57.040 --> 00:21:58.640
Hello?

279
00:22:01.360 --> 00:22:02.679
Is someone in there?

280
00:22:04.360 --> 00:22:06.479
Is that Barry?

281
00:22:06.480 --> 00:22:09.080
Because she's with Neville.
and it's not my fault.

282
00:22:19.000 --> 00:22:20.840
Sorry. I need to know who's in there.

283
00:22:23.480 --> 00:22:25.719
I'm coming in.

284
00:22:25.720 --> 00:22:27.040
Do you hear me?

285
00:22:30.080 --> 00:22:32.280
Make yourself... decent.

286
00:22:57.200 --> 00:23:00.720
If that's Barry. let's not make
this worse. Just say it's you.

287
00:23:42.960 --> 00:23:44.400
Hey!

288
00:24:26.240 --> 00:24:27.999
Hello.

289
00:24:28.000 --> 00:24:29.160
Hello.

290
00:24:35.280 --> 00:24:36.719
You scared me.

291
00:24:36.720 --> 00:24:37.960
You scared me.

292
00:25:11.800 --> 00:25:13.559
You're dead.

293
00:25:13.560 --> 00:25:15.360
You're dead.

294
00:25:29.360 --> 00:25:32.039
Hello. Bill.

295
00:25:37.480 --> 00:25:39.200
What's that?

296
00:25:47.000 --> 00:25:48.919
I'll tell you what it isn't.

297
00:25:48.920 --> 00:25:50.960
It isn't a freak optical effect...

298
00:26:00.160 --> 00:26:02.559
and it's following me.

299
00:26:09.640 --> 00:26:11.520
No. no. what are you doing?

300
00:26:12.840 --> 00:26:15.959
I'll tell you what. let's
just pop into my box.

301
00:26:15.960 --> 00:26:19.399
Your box? What good is getting
in your box going to do?

302
00:26:19.400 --> 00:26:22.280
What an extraordinarily long and
involved answer this is going to be.

303
00:26:25.280 --> 00:26:27.439
How do we stop it getting in?
We're trapped in here!

304
00:26:27.440 --> 00:26:29.439
Nothing gets through these doors.

305
00:26:29.440 --> 00:26:31.079
They're made of wood.

306
00:26:31.080 --> 00:26:32.880
They've got windows!

307
00:26:38.120 --> 00:26:40.599
Look. this is all mad. I know.

308
00:26:40.600 --> 00:26:43.560
But that's the girl I
told you about Heather...

309
00:26:44.680 --> 00:26:47.200
only I don't think it's really her.

310
00:26:49.440 --> 00:26:50.919
I know this is hard to believe.

311
00:26:50.920 --> 00:26:53.480
I know you're not exactly
a sci-fi person...

312
00:26:57.040 --> 00:26:59.920
Time And Relative Dimension In Space.

313
00:27:02.480 --> 00:27:04.720
TARDIS for short.

314
00:27:07.640 --> 00:27:09.759
You're safe in here.

315
00:27:09.760 --> 00:27:11.960
You're safe in here and
you always will be.

316
00:27:18.680 --> 00:27:20.000
Any questions?

317
00:27:23.960 --> 00:27:25.760
Is this a knock-through?

318
00:27:26.880 --> 00:27:28.160
Well. in a way. yes.

319
00:27:30.600 --> 00:27:31.960
Look at this place.

320
00:27:34.040 --> 00:27:35.891
- It's like a...
- ..spaceship.

321
00:27:35.893 --> 00:27:37.321
Kitchen.

322
00:27:37.400 --> 00:27:39.839
- A what?
- A really posh kitchen. all metal.

323
00:27:39.840 --> 00:27:42.559
What happened with the doors. though?
Did you run out of money?

324
00:27:42.560 --> 00:27:47.439
What you are standing in
is a technological marvel.

325
00:27:47.440 --> 00:27:49.720
It is science beyond magic.

326
00:27:51.520 --> 00:27:56.160
This is the gateway to everything
that ever was... or ever can be.

327
00:27:58.640 --> 00:28:00.040
Can I use the toilet?

328
00:28:01.600 --> 00:28:04.239
- Pardon?
- I've had a fright.

329
00:28:04.240 --> 00:28:05.919
I need the toilet.

330
00:28:05.920 --> 00:28:09.759
It's down there. first right. second
left. past the macaroon dispenser.

331
00:28:09.760 --> 00:28:10.879
Thanks.

332
00:28:10.880 --> 00:28:14.839
Human! Human alert. Do
you want me to repel her?

333
00:28:14.840 --> 00:28:17.319
She's just passing through.
She wants to use the toilet.

334
00:28:17.320 --> 00:28:19.679
I'd give it a minute if I were you.

335
00:28:19.680 --> 00:28:21.599
What was that?

336
00:28:21.600 --> 00:28:24.919
We have an incursion on campus.
Extra-terrestrial.

337
00:28:24.920 --> 00:28:26.280
We're under attack.

338
00:28:28.000 --> 00:28:29.520
Let's move.

339
00:28:31.600 --> 00:28:34.599
My God! This isn't
just a room. is it?

340
00:28:34.600 --> 00:28:36.879
No. it's not just a room.

341
00:28:36.880 --> 00:28:38.080
This is a lift!

342
00:28:43.880 --> 00:28:45.560
Well. come on. then.

343
00:28:56.960 --> 00:28:59.920
No interference here. as far as
I can see. The vault's secure.

344
00:29:02.200 --> 00:29:03.840
So your box can move?

345
00:29:05.000 --> 00:29:06.719
It can go anywhere it likes?

346
00:29:06.720 --> 00:29:08.879
Good. isn't it?

347
00:29:08.880 --> 00:29:10.999
Anywhere at all. in
the whole university?

348
00:29:11.000 --> 00:29:14.360
Is it my imagination. or is
this taking longer than normal?

349
00:29:17.200 --> 00:29:19.279
Hang on.

350
00:29:19.280 --> 00:29:21.559
The room's still inside the box.

351
00:29:21.560 --> 00:29:24.399
- This isn't a knock-through.
- Nope.

352
00:29:24.400 --> 00:29:27.639
Doctor! It's bigger on the inside
than it is on the outside!

353
00:29:27.640 --> 00:29:29.360
Wey-hey! We got there!

354
00:29:31.520 --> 00:29:34.759
How is that possible?
How do you do that?

355
00:29:34.760 --> 00:29:38.399
Well. first. you have to
imagine a very big box

356
00:29:38.400 --> 00:29:41.279
fitting inside a very small box.

357
00:29:41.280 --> 00:29:44.919
- OK.
- Then you have to make one.

358
00:29:44.920 --> 00:29:47.039
It's the second part people
normally get stuck on.

359
00:29:47.040 --> 00:29:48.999
Can we shut up. please? Busy. busy.

360
00:29:49.000 --> 00:29:51.119
I need to know if there's any
interest in what's inside

361
00:29:51.120 --> 00:29:53.839
- this vault.
- Why. what's inside it?

362
00:29:53.840 --> 00:29:56.199
Something I don't want anyone
being too curious about.

363
00:29:56.200 --> 00:29:58.199
So you put it in the
middle of a university?

364
00:29:58.200 --> 00:30:02.399
Ooh. valid point. Yeah. nice.

365
00:30:02.400 --> 00:30:05.199
Either the creature came here
specifically for what's in here.

366
00:30:05.200 --> 00:30:07.879
- or it's just a coincidence.
- It's just a coincidence.

367
00:30:07.880 --> 00:30:09.759
Well. we can't know that for sure.

368
00:30:09.760 --> 00:30:13.159
Yeah. we can. It was here for
ages before it did anything.

369
00:30:13.160 --> 00:30:15.879
If it had work to do. why would
it lie around in a puddle?

370
00:30:15.880 --> 00:30:19.559
- I don't know. maybe it's a student.
- Banter.

371
00:30:19.560 --> 00:30:20.960
It's good. this.

372
00:30:22.360 --> 00:30:23.519
Your go again.

373
00:30:30.560 --> 00:30:32.160
Nardole...

374
00:30:34.440 --> 00:30:38.560
we need to move away from the
doors and towards the TARDIS.

375
00:31:12.880 --> 00:31:14.440
What if it attacks us?

376
00:31:17.280 --> 00:31:19.159
Well. that's good news.

377
00:31:19.160 --> 00:31:21.439
It means it's not interested
in what's inside the vault.

378
00:31:21.440 --> 00:31:23.319
It just wants to kill us.

379
00:31:30.840 --> 00:31:32.200
Run!

380
00:31:33.800 --> 00:31:37.039
It's not interested in the
vault. it's chasing us.

381
00:31:37.040 --> 00:31:38.519
Let's give it a proper challenge.

382
00:31:38.520 --> 00:31:41.479
let's see how far she's prepared to go.

383
00:31:41.480 --> 00:31:43.960
But what about my friend. what
about Heather? Can you save her?

384
00:31:45.600 --> 00:31:48.560
First things first. Let's
see if we can survive her.

385
00:32:11.920 --> 00:32:13.599
But...

386
00:32:13.600 --> 00:32:14.919
Yes.

387
00:32:14.920 --> 00:32:16.800
- We've moved again.
- We have.

388
00:32:18.160 --> 00:32:19.319
- It was night.
- Yep.

389
00:32:19.320 --> 00:32:22.760
Now it's... day.

390
00:32:23.760 --> 00:32:27.559
- Definitely day.
- My God! Have we travelled in time?

391
00:32:27.560 --> 00:32:30.680
No. of course not. We've
travelled to Australia.

392
00:32:43.440 --> 00:32:45.480
- How are you doing?
- How do you think?

393
00:32:51.160 --> 00:32:52.480
Right. um...

394
00:32:54.840 --> 00:32:56.000
How do I help?

395
00:32:57.120 --> 00:32:59.359
- Can I ask you a personal question?
- No.

396
00:32:59.360 --> 00:33:02.039
- Can I anyway?
- Yes.

397
00:33:02.040 --> 00:33:03.559
Are you from space?

398
00:33:03.560 --> 00:33:05.559
No. of course not.

399
00:33:05.560 --> 00:33:07.439
Nobody's from space.

400
00:33:07.440 --> 00:33:09.519
I'm from a planet like everybody else.

401
00:33:09.520 --> 00:33:11.280
This planet?

402
00:33:12.440 --> 00:33:15.080
- No. not specifically this one.
- Doesn't make sense. then.

403
00:33:16.760 --> 00:33:17.959
What doesn't?

404
00:33:17.960 --> 00:33:21.119
TARDIS. If you're from another
planet. why would you name your box

405
00:33:21.120 --> 00:33:24.399
in English? Those initials wouldn't
work in any other language!

406
00:33:24.400 --> 00:33:27.159
- People don't generally bring that up.
- It looks like a phone box.

407
00:33:27.160 --> 00:33:31.159
Yes. well. that's the cloaking device.
It sort of hides itself.

408
00:33:31.160 --> 00:33:33.639
It's hidden itself as a box with
"pull to enter" on the front?

409
00:33:33.640 --> 00:33:37.640
It's stuck. It's supposed
to blend in. but it's broken.

410
00:33:48.040 --> 00:33:49.520
Doctor...

411
00:33:50.880 --> 00:33:53.439
Out. out. everybody out. shark attack!

412
00:33:58.840 --> 00:34:00.159
Where are we going?

413
00:34:00.160 --> 00:34:02.879
As far as we can. She made
Australia in a minute

414
00:34:02.880 --> 00:34:04.679
let's see what she can really do.

415
00:34:04.680 --> 00:34:07.119
Sir. we're leaving Earth.
What about the vault?

416
00:34:07.120 --> 00:34:08.439
We're fine.

417
00:34:08.440 --> 00:34:10.759
If there's any trouble.
I'll get a message on this.

418
00:34:10.760 --> 00:34:13.559
Let's see how long it
takes her to get here.

419
00:34:13.560 --> 00:34:14.840
Where are we?

420
00:34:16.040 --> 00:34:17.560
Other end of the universe.

421
00:34:18.720 --> 00:34:23.800
23 million years in the future.

422
00:34:26.520 --> 00:34:29.080
Yes. it's a time machine too.

423
00:34:52.200 --> 00:34:55.159
So this is... somewhere else?

424
00:34:55.160 --> 00:34:56.879
This is a different planet?

425
00:34:56.880 --> 00:34:58.679
Not Earth. a different one?

426
00:34:58.680 --> 00:35:00.400
That's the general idea.

427
00:35:03.800 --> 00:35:06.679
That's different sky? Is it
made of something different?

428
00:35:06.680 --> 00:35:08.271
- What is sky made of?
- Lemon drops.

429
00:35:08.273 --> 00:35:09.198
Really?

430
00:35:09.200 --> 00:35:11.119
No. but wouldn't that be nice?

431
00:35:11.120 --> 00:35:14.199
You can be very silly
sometimes. do you know that?

432
00:35:14.200 --> 00:35:18.279
So how do we know this... water
thing is actually dangerous?

433
00:35:18.280 --> 00:35:20.599
Because most things are.

434
00:35:20.600 --> 00:35:22.679
- That's true.
- Why? Is everything out here evil?

435
00:35:22.680 --> 00:35:26.199
Hardly anything is evil. but
most things are hungry.

436
00:35:26.200 --> 00:35:28.719
Hunger looks very like evil from
the wrong end of the cutlery.

437
00:35:28.720 --> 00:35:31.479
Or do you think that your bacon
sandwich loves you back?

438
00:35:31.480 --> 00:35:34.359
So what is it and what
was it doing on Earth?

439
00:35:34.360 --> 00:35:38.439
Well. there were scorch marks on
the concrete where we found it.

440
00:35:38.440 --> 00:35:40.679
Could have been left by a shuttle craft.

441
00:35:40.680 --> 00:35:43.679
The puddle. what did it look like?

442
00:35:43.680 --> 00:35:45.520
If that was a car. what
would you say that was?

443
00:35:46.840 --> 00:35:48.000
An oil leak?

444
00:35:49.040 --> 00:35:51.359
So it's space engine oil?

445
00:35:51.360 --> 00:35:53.999
Intelligent oil. Super
intelligent space oil.

446
00:35:54.000 --> 00:35:57.119
No. part of the ship itself.
Shape-shifting fluid that becomes

447
00:35:57.120 --> 00:35:58.400
anything it needs to be.

448
00:35:59.520 --> 00:36:00.679
Seriously?

449
00:36:00.680 --> 00:36:03.479
But it spent ages laying around.
being a puddle. what changed?

450
00:36:03.480 --> 00:36:05.439
Your friend.

451
00:36:05.440 --> 00:36:08.079
She looked into it. didn't she?
More than once.

452
00:36:08.080 --> 00:36:09.679
So?

453
00:36:09.680 --> 00:36:13.079
Maybe it saw something it needed.
What was she like. your friend?

454
00:36:13.080 --> 00:36:15.240
What did she want? What did she need?

455
00:36:16.680 --> 00:36:18.840
Everywhere I go. I just want to leave.

456
00:36:22.120 --> 00:36:23.999
I think she wanted to leave.

457
00:36:24.000 --> 00:36:25.200
You see?

458
00:36:26.480 --> 00:36:28.559
The puddle found a passenger.

459
00:36:28.560 --> 00:36:31.919
A left-behind droplet
of a liquid spaceship.

460
00:36:31.920 --> 00:36:36.039
A single tear drop. alone
in a strange world.

461
00:36:36.040 --> 00:36:39.919
Then. one day. it finds someone
who wants to fly away.

462
00:36:39.920 --> 00:36:41.279
Not just a passenger.

463
00:36:41.280 --> 00:36:44.840
more than a passenger it found
a pilot. so it ate her.

464
00:36:46.480 --> 00:36:50.319
- So why is it chasing this one?
- Everything wants. everything needs.

465
00:36:50.320 --> 00:36:52.079
But why does it want her?

466
00:36:52.080 --> 00:36:54.559
I don't know. I don't
know everything. Nardole.

467
00:36:54.560 --> 00:36:57.679
- I don't have it all written down.
- You act like you do.

468
00:36:57.680 --> 00:37:01.679
- I act like I do. because I don't.
- It must be looking for something.

469
00:37:01.680 --> 00:37:04.439
- Of course it is. everything is.
- But what?

470
00:37:04.440 --> 00:37:07.839
What. in the end are
any of us looking for?

471
00:37:07.840 --> 00:37:11.320
We're looking for someone
who's looking for us.

472
00:37:13.400 --> 00:37:15.400
Hey. still making eyes at a puddle?

473
00:37:18.880 --> 00:37:20.640
Bill!

474
00:37:21.800 --> 00:37:23.120
Bill!

475
00:37:24.120 --> 00:37:25.599
Quick!

476
00:37:25.600 --> 00:37:27.040
Back to the TARDIS!

477
00:37:33.160 --> 00:37:37.600
OK. it's fast. It time
travels. it never gives up.

478
00:37:39.400 --> 00:37:41.599
Plan! Basic sterilisation.

479
00:37:41.600 --> 00:37:43.999
We're going to run that thing
through the deadliest fire

480
00:37:44.000 --> 00:37:46.799
- in the universe.
- Yes. that sounds excellent.

481
00:37:46.800 --> 00:37:50.359
The deadliest fire in the universe.
That's definitely good.

482
00:37:50.360 --> 00:37:51.520
How do we do that?

483
00:37:51.522 --> 00:37:53.324
The only way we can. We
run through it first.

484
00:37:53.326 --> 00:37:54.350
Less good now.

485
00:37:56.960 --> 00:37:59.680
No. not there. I don't like it there!

486
00:38:02.120 --> 00:38:04.600
- Nardole!
- I don't like there.

487
00:38:07.480 --> 00:38:09.919
I want you running interference.
Can you do that?

488
00:38:09.920 --> 00:38:11.408
- Can I say no. sir?
- No.

489
00:38:11.473 --> 00:38:12.679
- Yes. then.
- Thank you.

490
00:38:12.680 --> 00:38:15.199
- But no really.
- Where are we?

491
00:38:15.200 --> 00:38:17.319
Well. we're basically
in the middle of a war.

492
00:38:17.320 --> 00:38:21.319
No... Well. it's a war zone. and
this is just your basic skirmish.

493
00:38:21.320 --> 00:38:23.959
and it's not as bad as it
sounds. I promise you.

494
00:38:23.960 --> 00:38:27.047
Come on. I've got friends
here. old friends.

495
00:38:27.760 --> 00:38:29.599
I say friends...

496
00:38:29.600 --> 00:38:32.679
The Doctor is detected.

497
00:38:32.680 --> 00:38:34.119
Seek. Locate.

498
00:38:34.120 --> 00:38:35.840
Destroy.

499
00:38:38.240 --> 00:38:41.719
- Are we still in the future?
- No. This is the past.

500
00:38:41.720 --> 00:38:44.600
Doesn't... look like the past.

501
00:38:45.880 --> 00:38:46.885
Are we safe here?

502
00:38:46.887 --> 00:38:49.841
Well. that's up to
Nardole. so probably not.

503
00:38:51.600 --> 00:38:53.560
I don't...

504
00:38:54.640 --> 00:38:57.119
I don't...

505
00:38:57.120 --> 00:38:59.039
- Keep moving. Doctor!
- Where are we going?

506
00:38:59.040 --> 00:39:00.679
Into the fire. come on.

507
00:39:11.840 --> 00:39:13.440
Who are those guys?

508
00:39:15.880 --> 00:39:18.960
Never mind them. it's
who they're firing at.

509
00:39:31.600 --> 00:39:33.000
Come on.

510
00:39:36.440 --> 00:39:38.839
- What's that?
- The deadliest fire in the universe.

511
00:39:38.840 --> 00:39:42.280
Identify intruder. Identify.

512
00:39:43.400 --> 00:39:44.919
Scan this device and identify me!

513
00:39:44.920 --> 00:39:48.079
You are the Doctor. You are
an enemy of the Daleks!

514
00:39:48.080 --> 00:39:50.880
- Yes. I am!
- Exterminate!

515
00:39:53.360 --> 00:39:54.959
Exterminate.

516
00:39:54.960 --> 00:39:56.760
Exterminate!

517
00:39:57.880 --> 00:39:59.520
Exterminate.

518
00:40:02.000 --> 00:40:04.720
Exterminate!

519
00:40:09.120 --> 00:40:10.761
- What was that thing?
- A Dalek.

520
00:40:10.774 --> 00:40:12.118
- A what?
- A Dalek.

521
00:40:12.120 --> 00:40:15.600
- What's a Dalek?
- Never mind. it's a Dalek.

522
00:40:16.840 --> 00:40:18.480
Exterminate!

523
00:40:25.680 --> 00:40:28.479
Exterminate...

524
00:40:28.480 --> 00:40:32.680
That's wrong. I know my
Daleks. and that's wrong.

525
00:40:36.680 --> 00:40:38.959
I see.

526
00:40:38.960 --> 00:40:40.319
You see what?

527
00:40:40.320 --> 00:40:42.639
I've sealed the area. all the
Daleks are quarantined...

528
00:40:42.640 --> 00:40:44.399
except that one.

529
00:40:44.400 --> 00:40:46.119
It's OK. This isn't a Dalek.

530
00:40:46.120 --> 00:40:48.079
Look.

531
00:40:48.080 --> 00:40:49.440
Look at the eye.

532
00:40:50.480 --> 00:40:51.800
Heather.

533
00:41:10.352 --> 00:41:11.391
Heather.

534
00:41:11.393 --> 00:41:15.141
Interesting. you had a gun
but you didn't use it. Why?

535
00:41:15.360 --> 00:41:17.599
You've already taken one
person from the Earth.

536
00:41:17.600 --> 00:41:20.559
I'm going to let that
pass. because I have to.

537
00:41:20.560 --> 00:41:22.760
but I will not let you take another.

538
00:41:24.440 --> 00:41:25.840
Go.

539
00:41:27.240 --> 00:41:29.840
Just go. now. Fly away.

540
00:41:35.560 --> 00:41:37.240
Why won't you just go?

541
00:41:44.800 --> 00:41:46.679
Promise you won't go?

542
00:41:46.680 --> 00:41:47.960
Promise.

543
00:41:49.320 --> 00:41:52.479
My God. I understand.

544
00:41:52.480 --> 00:41:54.639
- You what?
- The last thing she said to me.

545
00:41:54.640 --> 00:41:56.999
She promised she wouldn't
leave without me.

546
00:41:57.000 --> 00:42:00.799
Her last conscious thought.
driving her across the universe.

547
00:42:00.800 --> 00:42:02.759
Never underestimate a crush.

548
00:42:02.760 --> 00:42:04.639
You don't have to tell me!

549
00:42:04.640 --> 00:42:06.759
What do we do?

550
00:42:06.760 --> 00:42:08.639
I don't know.

551
00:42:08.640 --> 00:42:12.279
She's not chasing you.
she's inviting you.

552
00:42:12.280 --> 00:42:13.919
Release her.

553
00:42:13.920 --> 00:42:16.640
Release her from her promise.

554
00:42:27.080 --> 00:42:29.199
You have to let me go.

555
00:42:29.200 --> 00:42:30.640
You have to let me go.

556
00:42:32.160 --> 00:42:33.799
I will.

557
00:42:33.800 --> 00:42:35.040
I will.

558
00:42:42.520 --> 00:42:44.319
I really liked you.

559
00:42:44.320 --> 00:42:46.160
I really liked you.

560
00:42:55.680 --> 00:42:57.320
Bill...

561
00:42:58.520 --> 00:43:00.359
don't. don't!

562
00:43:00.360 --> 00:43:01.799
Don't do that!

563
00:43:01.800 --> 00:43:04.400
Listen. please. just listen to him.

564
00:43:07.920 --> 00:43:10.040
Don't. don't! Bill. let go!

565
00:43:11.920 --> 00:43:14.119
Bill. listen to me.

566
00:43:14.120 --> 00:43:16.679
Whatever she's showing you.
whatever she's letting you see.

567
00:43:16.680 --> 00:43:19.679
It's a lure. it's a trap.

568
00:43:19.680 --> 00:43:23.039
She's making you part of her.
and you can never come back.

569
00:43:23.040 --> 00:43:25.160
I see what you see.

570
00:43:28.080 --> 00:43:30.079
It's beautiful.

571
00:43:30.080 --> 00:43:32.479
Bill. let go! You have to let go!

572
00:43:32.480 --> 00:43:34.800
She is not human any more.

573
00:43:37.080 --> 00:43:38.640
Goodbye. Heather.

574
00:43:41.280 --> 00:43:44.200
Goodbye... Bill.

575
00:43:48.920 --> 00:43:50.400
Bill!

576
00:43:59.760 --> 00:44:01.320
You all right?

577
00:44:03.120 --> 00:44:04.640
Yeah. I think so.

578
00:44:13.520 --> 00:44:15.159
You don't look all right.

579
00:44:15.160 --> 00:44:16.400
She's fine.

580
00:44:17.880 --> 00:44:21.760
That's the Doctor for you.
Never notices the tears.

581
00:44:30.240 --> 00:44:32.440
I don't think they're mine.

582
00:44:40.800 --> 00:44:43.079
The vault alarm went
off. but it was nothing.

583
00:44:43.080 --> 00:44:47.200
A student was sick outside and it
registered as a biological attack.

584
00:44:49.320 --> 00:44:50.920
I saw it all for a moment...

585
00:44:52.200 --> 00:44:53.879
everything out there.

586
00:44:53.880 --> 00:44:56.879
She was going to let me fly with her.
She was inviting me.

587
00:44:56.880 --> 00:44:59.200
- But I was too scared.
- Scared is good.

588
00:45:00.440 --> 00:45:03.599
Scared is rational. She
wasn't human any more.

589
00:45:03.600 --> 00:45:05.120
Will we see her again?

590
00:45:07.040 --> 00:45:08.560
I don't see how.

591
00:45:14.880 --> 00:45:17.479
No. no. no. No. no. You
have to forget about that.

592
00:45:17.480 --> 00:45:18.640
I don't see how I can.

593
00:45:20.040 --> 00:45:21.600
I do.

594
00:45:23.920 --> 00:45:25.120
Come here. Bill.

595
00:45:27.600 --> 00:45:29.559
What's up?

596
00:45:29.560 --> 00:45:32.519
- I just want to fix something.
- Whoa. what are you doing?

597
00:45:32.520 --> 00:45:35.023
- Don't worry. This won't hurt at all.
- No. but tell me.

598
00:45:35.262 --> 00:45:36.918
Nothing.

599
00:45:36.920 --> 00:45:39.280
Yeah. cos I think you're
going to wipe my memory.

600
00:45:40.640 --> 00:45:42.639
I'm not stupid. you know.

601
00:45:42.640 --> 00:45:44.399
That's the trouble with you.

602
00:45:44.400 --> 00:45:46.439
You don't think anyone's
ever seen a movie.

603
00:45:46.440 --> 00:45:48.679
- I know what a mind-wipe looks like!
- I have no choice.

604
00:45:48.680 --> 00:45:53.119
I'm here for a reason. I'm in disguise.
I have promises to keep.

605
00:45:53.120 --> 00:45:55.719
No-one can know about me.

606
00:45:55.720 --> 00:45:57.319
This is the most exciting thing

607
00:45:57.320 --> 00:46:00.359
that's ever happened to me in my life.
The only exciting thing!

608
00:46:00.360 --> 00:46:01.760
I'm sorry.

609
00:46:02.960 --> 00:46:06.959
OK. Let me remember just for a week.
Just a week.

610
00:46:06.960 --> 00:46:09.399
OK. well. just for tonight.
Just one night.

611
00:46:09.400 --> 00:46:12.040
Come on. let me have some
good dreams for once.

612
00:46:15.640 --> 00:46:16.960
OK.

613
00:46:19.240 --> 00:46:21.120
Do what you've got to do.

614
00:46:23.560 --> 00:46:24.720
But imagine...

615
00:46:26.160 --> 00:46:29.480
just imagine how it would feel
if someone did this to you.

616
00:46:45.120 --> 00:46:46.919
- Get out!
- What?

617
00:46:46.920 --> 00:46:50.039
You can keep your memories. Now
get out before I change my mind!

618
00:46:50.040 --> 00:46:54.080
Don't speak. don't start. just run!
Now. Go!

619
00:47:01.720 --> 00:47:03.279
Shut up.

620
00:47:03.280 --> 00:47:04.519
You shut up as well.

621
00:47:07.320 --> 00:47:10.039
Will you all please just leave me alone?

622
00:47:10.040 --> 00:47:12.120
I can't do that any more. I promised!

623
00:47:38.920 --> 00:47:43.160
It's a big universe. but maybe
one day we'll find her.

624
00:47:52.880 --> 00:47:54.600
What changed your mind?

625
00:47:59.120 --> 00:48:00.400
Time...

626
00:48:02.480 --> 00:48:04.200
Time?

627
00:48:06.560 --> 00:48:08.880
And Relative Dimension In Space.

628
00:48:20.000 --> 00:48:21.879
It means...

629
00:48:21.880 --> 00:48:24.160
what the hell?!

630
00:48:35.120 --> 00:48:37.119
This is one of Earth's first colonies.

631
00:48:37.120 --> 00:48:39.679
- What are they? Alien birds?
- Tiny robots.

632
00:48:39.680 --> 00:48:43.119
That is a robot. It speaks emoji!

633
00:48:43.120 --> 00:48:44.759
And where are all the people?

634
00:48:44.760 --> 00:48:46.119
Argh!

635
00:48:46.120 --> 00:48:47.279
What. you're going back in?

636
00:48:47.280 --> 00:48:49.440
I'm having this really childish
impulse to blow it up.

637
00:48:54.000 --> 00:48:56.239
- You're the one who should be afraid.
- Never.

638
00:48:56.240 --> 00:48:57.919
Get ready.

639
00:48:59.560 --> 00:49:01.279
I'm the Doctor.

640
00:49:01.880 --> 00:49:05.239
I've been standing by the gates of
your world. keeping you all safe.

641
00:49:05.740 --> 00:49:07.340
I'm not stopping now. Any questions?

642
00:49:08.241 --> 00:49:14.241
- Sync and corrections by Doctor C -
- www.addic7ed.com -
